Z||000000||Motorhead||01-18-2001||07:10 PM||||I passed a great looking silver GT in Myrtle Beach today at Hwy 501 and 17 bypass.  Honked the horn and waved! Was that anyone on the Forum?<BR>I thought there was only two of us here at the beach, but thought I'd ask.<BR>Mike<P><P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||turbo86se||01-19-2001||02:29 PM||||Mike, the only silver '87 GT in Myrtle Beach I've ever seen is owned by a gentleman that lives off Forrestbrook Road. He's got two MINT very low-mileage 87GT's in his garage. Both covered, one silver the other black. I drive by his house a good bit, and lately I've seen the silver one out. My mechanic has done some minor work to that one.<BR> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||01-19-2001||05:04 PM||||This was a young guy.  If I hadn't been in such a hurry I would have flagged him down and talked. <BR>I noticed the black GT in Little River that was for sale is gone.  Wonder who got it?<BR>  <P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||01-20-2001||12:13 AM||||The black GT in Little River, I drove that car! I've got a picture of it around here somewhere, that was a sweet car. I think someone in NC got it. The owner was real nice, with a real cute daughter!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you're ever in Latta, check out the AWESOME '84 Indy sitting at an automobile repair shop on 501, just a few miles south of the border. Too bad it's not for sale.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
